  "browserSchemaVersion": 5,
  "localChanges": "The separate Ichimoku lecture scope and selected-timeframe rules remain intact. The mixed Watchlist now selects the sibling crypto project’s twelve 29 September 2026 paper profiles on independent completed 1d and 4h sources, with source-derived directional feature gates and fixed or managed paper reference plans. It excludes the historical harmonic, trend and independent-method roster from mixed results, removes the mixed display cap, and screens frozen plans without assuming the next whole one-minute opening, intervening minute checks or a fill. Cloud targets remain original structural references until an execution-time net-2R cap can be checked. Browser history is bounded to 500 completed candles per frame, unlike the sibling project’s full stored contiguous source. The old frozen Go source hash is retained; local ports and fixtures are identified below.",
